/*
 * Container overrides for vendored nf-core modules.
 *
 * This file exists to work around ONE upstream packaging bug and should be
 * deleted, along with its `includeConfig` line in nextflow.config, as soon
 * as that bug is out of the installed modules. It is deliberately separate
 * from conf/modules.config, which carries `ext.args` and `ext.prefix` only,
 * so the deviation stays visible rather than buried among per-process args.
 *
 * THE BUG. The nf-core `simpleaf/index` and `simpleaf/quant` modules pin
 * simpleaf 0.25.0 with alevin-fry 0.15.0. alevin-fry at tag v0.15.0 ships
 * a `.cargo/config.toml` containing `rustflags = ["-C", "target-cpu=native"]`,
 * and the bioconda recipe builds it with a plain `cargo install --path .`,
 * so the published binary is tuned to whatever CPU the build worker had.
 * On any CPU with fewer features it aborts with SIGILL on startup — even
 * `alevin-fry --version` dies. `simpleaf set-paths` shells out to exactly
 * that, so it exits 1 and takes the whole task with it: neither simpleaf
 * process can run at all. Reproduced here on a Zen 2 host (avx, avx2,
 * bmi2, no AVX-512).
 *
 * THE FIX, upstream. alevin-fry commit 0e13d52 (2026-07-10), "make
 * .cargo/config.toml portable by default (drop target-cpu=native)",
 * replaces it with the portable `target-cpu=x86-64-v3 -C target-feature=+avx2`
 * baseline. alevin-fry 0.18.1 carries that fix, and bioconda's simpleaf
 * 0.30.0 recipe requires `alevin-fry >=0.18.1` and `piscem >=0.23.0`.
 *
 * THE IMAGE. quay.io/biocontainers/simpleaf:0.30.0--hd612981_0 contains
 * simpleaf 0.30.0, alevin-fry 0.18.1 and piscem 0.23.0. Verified by
 * running it: `simpleaf set-paths` exits 0 on the host the pinned image
 * fails on. Its CLI is compatible with the vendored modules' script
 * blocks — every flag they pass still exists — and its chemistry registry
 * is identical to 0.25.0's, `10xv4-3p` included.
 *
 * WHEN TO DELETE THIS FILE. When `nf-core modules update simpleaf/index
 * simpleaf/quant` brings in a module whose environment.yml requires
 * alevin-fry 0.18.1 or newer. Check the alevin-fry pin in the two
 * `environment.yml` files under `modules/nf-core/simpleaf/`.
 *
 * Do NOT instead edit the vendored modules; they are never modified.
 */

process {
    withName: 'SIMPLEAF_INDEX|SIMPLEAF_QUANT' {
        container = 'quay.io/biocontainers/simpleaf:0.30.0--hd612981_0'
    }
}
